## 6.7 Real-World Scenario Stress Tests

Both models were stress-tested against six scenarios calibrated to real measured signal levels from the Mangalore dataset.

**Table 6.16: XGBoost — Spatial Scenario Predictions**

| Scenario | Risk Probability | Label |
|---|---|---|
| 🌀 Extreme cyclone SSCS (all sensors maxed) | 94.8% | 🔴 HIGH |
| 🌧️ Cyclone landfall (coastal, low elevation) | 92.1% | 🔴 HIGH |
| 🌊 High tide + monsoon surge (June peak) | 93.5% | 🔴 HIGH |
| 🏖️ Panambur beach zone (low elev, tidal) | 91.7% | 🔴 HIGH |
| 🏙️ Mangalore city core (poor drainage) | 12.6% | 🟢 SAFE |
| ⛅ Post-monsoon (Oct calm) | 0.0% | 🟢 SAFE |
| 🏔️ Kadri Hills safe zone (high elevation) | 0.0% | 🟢 SAFE |

**Table 6.17: LSTM — Temporal Scenario Predictions (12-step / 6h window)**

| Scenario | Risk Probability | Label |
|---|---|---|
| 🌀 Extreme cyclone surge (all sensors maxed) | 96.2% | 🔴 HIGH |
| 🌧️ June monsoon burst (peak rain + tide) | 94.5% | 🔴 HIGH |
| 🌊 Tidal surge — Mangalore port zone | 93.8% | 🔴 HIGH |
| 💧 River Netravathi at flood warning level | 92.9% | 🔴 HIGH |
| ⛅ Post-storm drain-down (Oct lull) | 0.0% | 🟢 SAFE |
| ☀️ Dry season baseline (Jan–Mar) | 0.0% | 🟢 SAFE |

Both models demonstrate correct discrimination across all tested scenarios with no false positives or false negatives under extreme conditions. The XGBoost model correctly identifies that the urban city core is SAFE despite poor drainage, as its SRTM elevation (> 10 m) places it outside confirmed flood zones — a geographically accurate result.

