## 6.8 Comparison with State of the Art

**Table 6.18: Comparison with Existing Flood Routing and Risk Methods**

| Method | Accuracy | Routing | Temporal Modelling | Multi-Unit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Bui et al. (2019) — Flood susceptibility mapping | 85.3% | No | No | N/A |
| Tehrany et al. (2015) — SVM flood mapping | 77.4% | No | No | N/A |
| Standard Dijkstra routing (no flood awareness) | N/A | Yes | No | No |
| Chen et al. (2021) — A\* flood-aware routing | N/A | Yes | No | Single unit |
| **Proposed System** | **90.00% (spatial)** | **Yes** | **Yes (LSTM, 87.06%)** | **Yes (GA-QUBO)** |

To the best of our knowledge, no existing published work simultaneously addresses spatial flood risk classification, temporal flood forecasting, and multi-agent flood-aware route optimisation in a unified real-time system. The proposed system is the first to:
1. Fuse live ERA5 rainfall, GloFAS river discharge, and marine tidal data into a single spatio-temporal flood map;
2. Benchmark the new deterministic O(m√log n) Tsinghua v2 SSSP algorithm (Duan et al. 2026) against classical routing algorithms on a real urban road network;
3. Apply a QUBO-formulated Genetic Algorithm for simultaneous multi-ambulance route conflict resolution.

